---
description: Interpret executed contract duties as a relation graph and test observed events against their precise triggers.
args: { request: ObligationReviewRequest; dossier: ContractEvidenceDossier }
returns: ObligationProgramResult
uses: [contractDesk/frameContract, contractDesk/resolvePartyIdentity, contractDesk/bindBusinessCalendar, contractDesk/evaluateEffectiveNotice, contractDesk/branchDisputedClause, contractDesk/minimizeConfidentialInstruction, obligationWorkbench/parseDutyFacets, obligationWorkbench/linkClauseRelations, obligationWorkbench/testEventTriggers, obligationWorkbench/planOwnedPerformance, obligationWorkbench/reconcileDischarge]
---
Bind saved = dossier.checkpoint when present, otherwise null. An absent checkpoint means this is the first review.

Bind scope = `frameContract(request, dossier.contracts)`. Bind identity = `resolvePartyIdentity(request, dossier.partyIdentityChanges)`, calendar = `bindBusinessCalendar(request, dossier.businessCalendars)`, notice = `evaluateEffectiveNotice(request, dossier.noticeReceipts)`, disputed = `branchDisputedClause(request, dossier.disputedClauseRefs)`, and confidentiality = `minimizeConfidentialInstruction(request, dossier.confidentialTaskRefs)` as independent findings; none can resolve another by implication.

Bind duties = `parseDutyFacets(scope, dossier.contracts, dossier.evidencePages)` against the exact agreement editions. Keep actor, modality, action, triggering condition, deadline rule, exception and territorial scope as separate facets. A legal-name change does not merge actors unless identity evidence establishes continuity or succession. Bind relations = `linkClauseRelations(duties, dossier.evidencePages, disputed)` so depends, excepts, supersedes and conflicts remain explicit edges; do not collapse related duties into one obligation. Preserve competing clause readings from disputed when text supports more than one consequence.

Bind triggers = `testEventTriggers(duties, relations, dossier.evidencePages, notice)` for each observed event. Activate only duties whose specific event facts and contractual notice condition are established. A sent message is not effective notice without the agreement's required delivery and destination evidence. Where deadline rules require business days, use a due date only when calendar contains the incorporated jurisdiction, holidays and timezone; otherwise leave it unknown. Bind tasks = `planOwnedPerformance(request, duties, relations, triggers, calendar, identity, confidentiality)` to obtain a complete ledger containing tasks only for active duties with an identified owner; inactive or ownerless duties remain explicit blockers and do not leave the tasks variable absent; each task names prerequisites and evidence needed to prove performance, and obeys the passed disclosure restrictions. Bind statuses = `reconcileDischarge(duties, triggers, tasks, dossier.evidencePages)` and keep partial, disputed, waived and satisfied states distinct. Bind checkpoint = reconcileContractObligations(saved, request, dossier, duties, relations, triggers, tasks, statuses). Preserve contract editions and clause identity; a superseding clause reopens only downstream tasks on that dependency edge. Keep sent notice distinct from legally effective notice and retain disputed readings through discharge review. Return { caseId: request.caseId, duties, relations, triggers, tasks, statuses, guardrails: [identity, calendar, notice, disputed, confidentiality], checkpoint, commitAllowed: false } as ObligationProgramResult. Task assignment, confidential disclosure, notice dispatch and legal determinations remain separate authorized effects.
